  "provider_query": "Jargon File entry that defines yak shaving",
  "answer": "**Jargon File entry (canonical)**\n\nFrom *The Jargon File* (catb.org), entry **yak shaving**:\n\n> **yak shaving**  \n> [MIT AI Lab, after 2000: orig. probably from a *Ren & Stimpy* episode.] Any seemingly pointless activity which is actually necessary to solve a problem which solves a problem which, several levels of recursion later, solves the real problem you're working on.\n\nSource: https://www.catb.org/jargon/html/Y/yak-shaving.html\n\n**Related results (up to 8)**\n\n1. **Jargon File (catb.org)** — Full short entry above; tags origin as MIT AI Lab after 2000, probably *Ren & Stimpy*. https://www.catb.org/jargon/html/Y/yak-shaving.html\n\n2. **Mirror of the same entry** — Same wording: “Any seemingly pointless activity which is actually necessary to solve a problem which solves a problem which, several levels of recursion later, solves the real problem you're working on.” http://underpop.free.fr/j/jargon/y/yak-shaving.html\n\n3. **ZVON index** — Points “yak shaving” at the Jargon File glossary of hacker slang. https://zvon.org/comp/m/yak_shaving.html\n\n4. **Jeremy H. Brown (MIT, 2000), via later write-ups** — Early written definition often cited alongside the Jargon File: a stupid, fiddly task whose link to the real work is only a long causal chain; attributes the coinage to Carlin Vieri. Summarized in https://www.levellers.ai/what-is/yak-shaving and https://lonesysadmin.net/tag/jargon-file/\n\n5. **TechTarget** — Programming slang for an endless series of small tasks before the next step can proceed; credits Carlin J. Vieri (MIT, 1990s) and *Ren & Stimpy*’s “Yak Shaving Day.” https://www.techtarget.com/whatis/definition/yak-shaving\n\n6. **Stack Exchange (Software Engineering)** — Matches the recursive “task needed for a task…” sense; notes both neutral (necessary chain) and negative (sidetrack) uses, and quotes Vieri on staying related to the primary objective. https://softwareengineering.stackexchange.com/questions/388092/what-exactly-is-yak-shaving\n\n7. **Visual Thesaurus** — “Annoying succession of tasks you need to accomplish in order to get to your actual goal”; cites MIT/Carlin Vieri and the Jargon File’s *Ren & Stimpy* link. https://www.visualthesaurus.com/cm/wc/heavy-lifting-and-shaving-yaks-corporate-lingo/\n\n8. **NetLingo** — Tedious tasks before productive work, or useless activity to avoid real work; origin around 2000 at MIT via *Ren & Stimpy*. https://www.netlingo.com/word/yak-shaving.php",
